hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"399","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last (to come) but will be the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. And we will be the first to enter Paradise. However, the fact is that the Book was given to those people before us and to us after them. And they differed regarding the truth. So this Friday is the day about which they differed, and Allah guided us. Thus, Friday is for us, the next day is for the Jews (i.e., Saturday), and the third day is for the Christians (i.e., Sunday, which they have fixed for themselves)."
"400","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun rises is Friday. On this day Adam (peace be upon him) was created, on this day he was admitted into Paradise, and on this day he was expelled from it. And the Day of Resurrection will also be established on this Friday."
"401","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is an hour on Friday during which, if a Muslim stands in prayer and asks Allah for something good, Allah will surely grant it to him."" And (the narrator said) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indicated with his hand that it is very brief, and he encouraged seeking it."
"402","´Sayyiduna Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa Ash'ari رضي الله عنه said that` Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar رضي الله عنهما said to me, ""Have you heard anything from your father about the hour of Jumu'ah which he narrated from the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم?"" I said, ""Yes, I heard from him."" He used to say that I heard the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم say, ""That hour is from when the Imam sits down for the sermon until the prayer is offered."
"403","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite ""Alif Lam Meem Sajdah"" and ""Hal Ata Alal Insan Hainum Minad Dahr"" in the Fajr prayer on Friday, and in the Friday prayer he used to recite Surah Al-Jumu'ah and Al-Munafiqun."
"404","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was delivering the Friday sermon to the people one day when Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) pointed towards him and said, ""What will be the state of those people who delay after the adhan?"" So Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Commander of the Faithful! When I heard the adhan, I did nothing except perform wudu; I performed wudu and came."" Sayyiduna Umar al-Faruq (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Did you only perform wudu? Did the people not hear that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say that when any of you comes for Jumu'ah, he must perform ghusl?"
"405","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bathing and using the miswak on Friday is obligatory upon every adult. And if perfume is available, it should also be applied."
"406","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the day of Jumu’ah, at every door of the mosque there are angels who write down (the names of) those who come, the first one who comes, then the one after him, then the one after him. Then when the Imam sits on the pulpit, the angels close their registers and come to listen to the sermon. And the example of the reward for the one who comes at the earliest time is like one who offers a camel in sacrifice. The one who comes after him is like one who offers a cow in sacrifice. The one who comes after him is like one who offers a ram in sacrifice. The one who comes after him is like one who offers a chicken in sacrifice. The one who comes after him is like one who offers an egg in the way of Allah."
"407","Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We used to perform Jumu’ah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when the sun had declined. Then we would return seeking shade (that is, there would be no shade of the walls)."
"408","Narrated from Abu Hazim: Some people came to Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) and began to argue about the pulpit—what kind of wood it was made from. He said: I know what kind of wood it was made from and who made it. And I saw when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat on it for the first time. (Abu Hazim says:) I said: O Abu Abbas! Tell us all about this. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent word to a woman (Abu Hazim said that Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned the name of this woman that day) that she should allow her slave, who was a carpenter, some time to make a few pieces of wood for me, that is, a pulpit on which I may speak to the people (that is, give sermons and advice). So her slave made a pulpit with three steps, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that it be placed in the mosque at that spot. Its wood was from the tamarisk of Ghabah (Ghabah is a place on the heights of Madinah), and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stand on it and say the takbir. The people also said the takbir behind him while he was on the pulpit. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head from bowing and stepped down backwards until he prostrated at the base of the pulpit. Then he returned to the pulpit until he finished the prayer. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned to the people and said: O people! I did this so that you may follow me and learn to pray as I pray."
"409","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Dhamad (this is the name of a person) came to Makkah and he was from the tribe of Azd Shanwah, and he used to perform ruqyah (spiritual healing) for those afflicted by jinn and evil spirits. He heard from the ignorant people of Makkah that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (God forbid) is possessed. So he said, ""I will see this person, perhaps Allah will cure him at my hands."" Thus, he met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! I perform ruqyah for the effects of jinn and such, and Allah grants healing to whom He wills at my hands. Do you wish for this?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""All praise is due to Allah, I praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides, none can misguide, and whomever He misguides, none can guide. And I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His servant and Messenger. Now, after the praise, say what you wish."" Dhamad said, ""Recite these words again."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited these words three times. Then Dhamad said, ""I have heard the words of soothsayers, I have heard the sayings of magicians, I have heard the poetry of poets, but I have never heard anything equal to these words, and these have reached the depths of eloquence."" Then Dhamad said, ""Give me your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to Islam."" So he pledged allegiance. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Shall I take the pledge from you on behalf of your people as well?"" He replied, ""Yes, I pledge allegiance on behalf of my people as well."" (The narrator says) Eventually, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a military detachment, and they passed by the people of Dhamad. The leader of that army said, ""Have you taken anything from this tribe?"" Then a man said, ""Yes, I have taken a water vessel from them."" He ordered, ""Go and return it, for this is the tribe of Dhamad (and they are under protection due to Dhamad's pledge)."
"410","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon, his eyes would become red, his voice would rise, and his anger would increase, as if he were warning of an approaching army, saying, ""The enemy is coming in the morning or in the evening."" And he would say: ""I and the Hour have been sent like these two,"" and he would join his index and middle fingers together. After praising and glorifying Allah, he would say: ""Know that the best speech is the Book of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The worst of affairs are newly invented matters, and every innovation in worship is misguidance."" Then he would say: ""I am closer to every believer than his own self. So if a believer dies and leaves behind wealth, it is for his family. But if he leaves behind debt or children, their care is my responsibility and their expenses are upon me."
"411","´Sayyiduna Abu Wa'il (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon to us, and it was very brief and extremely eloquent. Then when he descended from the pulpit, we said, ""O Abu al-Yaqzan! You delivered a very eloquent and extremely brief sermon. If you had made this sermon a bit longer, it would have been better."" Then Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man's prolonging of the prayer and shortening of the sermon is a sign of his understanding, so make the prayer long and the sermon short. And some speech is (as effective as) magic (i.e., it has an effect)."
"412","It is narrated from Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man delivered a sermon before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has found the right path, and whoever disobeys both of them has gone astray.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “What a bad speaker you are. Rather, say: ‘Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has gone astray.’”"
"413","Sayyida Umm Hisham bint Haritha bin Nu'man (may Allah be pleased with her) says: For two years, or a year and some months, our oven and the oven of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were the same. And I memorized Surah ""Qaf"" from the blessed tongue of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) because he used to recite it on the pulpit while delivering the sermon on Fridays."
"414","It is narrated from Husain that ‘Amarah bin Ru’aybah (may Allah be pleased with him) saw Bishr, the son of Marwan, on the pulpit raising both his hands (to gesture during the sermon). So he said, “May Allah ruin these two hands! I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do no more than this,” and he gestured with his index finger."
"415","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to deliver the sermon standing on the day of Jumu'ah. So once, a caravan came from Syria (bringing grain), and people rushed towards it, leaving only twelve men with the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. Upon this, the verse was revealed which is in Surah Al-Jumu'ah: ""When they see a trade or amusement, they rush towards it and leave you standing..."" the entire verse."
"416","Narrated by Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite ""Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High"" (Surah Al-A'la) and ""Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?"" (Surah Al-Ghashiyah) in the Eid and Friday prayers. And when Friday and Eid would fall on the same day, he would still recite these two Surahs in both prayers."
"417","‘Sayyiduna Abu Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon. He says: I submitted, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! A poor (traveler) man has come to ask about his religion and does not know what his religion is.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards me, left his sermon, and came to me. A chair was brought, and I think its legs were made of iron. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat on it (it is understood that sitting on a chair is not prohibited) and began to teach me what Allah had taught him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned and completed his sermon. (This was the perfection of his character, and it is understood that a necessary matter is permissible during the sermon.)"
"418","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would deliver the sermon standing. Then he would sit down, then stand up and deliver it standing. And whoever among you says that he used to deliver it sitting, by Allah, he has lied. And by Allah, I have offered more than two thousand prayers with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"419","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I have performed prayers with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). His prayer and sermon (both) were moderate. (That is, neither very long nor short.)"
"420","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sulaik Ghatafani came on the day of Jumu’ah while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting on the pulpit. Sulaik (may Allah be pleased with him) sat down without performing prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Have you prayed two rak‘ahs?"" He replied, ""No."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Stand up and perform them."
"421","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you say to your companion on the day of Jumu'ah, ""Be quiet,"" while the Imam is delivering the sermon, then you have engaged in idle talk."
"422","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: Whoever performs ghusl and comes for Jumu'ah, and prays as much as is destined for him, then remains silent until the sermon is finished, then prays with the Imam, then his sins from this Jumu'ah to the previous Jumu'ah and three additional days are forgiven."
"423","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have offered the Friday prayer, then perform four rak'ahs. In another narration, it is stated: If you are in a hurry, then perform two rak'ahs in the mosque and two rak'ahs after returning home."
"424","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when he (Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him) had finished offering Jumu'ah, he would come home and perform two rak'ahs and would say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same."
"425","‘Umar bin ‘Ata says that Sayyiduna Nafi‘ bin Jubayr sent him to Sayyiduna Sa’ib bin Akht Numayr to ask about the matter which Sayyiduna Mu‘awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) had noticed in his prayer. (When ‘Umar bin ‘Ata went and asked,) Sa’ib bin Akht Numayr said: Yes! I had performed the Friday prayer with him (Sayyiduna Mu‘awiyah, may Allah be pleased with him) at Maqsura (name of a place). When the Imam finished the prayer with salam, I stood at my place and started praying. Sayyiduna Mu‘awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for me after entering (the house or a room, etc.), and said: Do not do today what you did again in the future. When you finish the Friday prayer, do not perform another prayer immediately until you have spoken or left that place. Because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us this. (He, peace and blessings be upon him, said in this way) that after one prayer, we should not perform another prayer immediately without speaking or leaving that place."
"426","It is narrated from Hakam bin Mina that Abdullah bin Umar and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them) told him that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, while he was standing on the wooden pulpit: ""People must stop neglecting Jumu'ah, or else Allah will seal their hearts and they will become among the heedless."
